+- Not run on Windows. Nothing in this release depends on the operating system, but a check on Windows 10/11 is still worth doing.
+- The size in Settings is the font size in CSS pixels, as before; only its label changed. At 100% text zoom, 15 looks about like 11-point type in a word processor.
+- In source view a selection that cuts through Markdown syntax is counted as the text it would be on its own. Selecting only a link's address, or only the description inside an image, counts those words, although the document count leaves them out. The same can happen with single lines taken out of a table, a code block or another construct of several lines. In the sample `docs/test-documents/PicoMarQ-Torture-Test.md` (916 words) the blocks selected one at a time add up to exactly 916, the 144 lines selected one at a time to 924, and none of 3,000 random selections counted more words than a plain count of the selected characters.
+- Hyphenated words count as two words, in the selection as in the total (unchanged).
+- Found while writing the test, the same in 1.2.6 and 1.2.7, and not changed: in the first 0.15 s or so after leaving source view, the editor places the caret, and an arrow key pressed in that instant right after Ctrl+A can be ignored. Only a script is that fast; the status bar shows the selection the editor really has.
